  "notes": [
    "The API promotion for gpt-5.6-sol and its gpt-5.6 and gpt-daybreak-blue-latest aliases ends on 2026-11-30. Review those rates and the Bedrock IDs for the same models after that date.",
    "The published gpt-6-astra-law rates are promotional through at least 2026-12-31. Only Standard input, output and cached input rates are listed. Review after that date.",
    "The deprecated gpt-daybreak-blue-latest and gpt-daybreak-red-latest aliases currently resolve to gpt-5.6-sol and gpt-5.6-cyber, respectively.",
    "claude-sonnet-4-5 and claude-sonnet-4 now have a 200K window. Their long-context premium only prices older history.",
    "o3 keeps its Standard rates of 2/0.5/8 for input/cache reads/output, matching the pricing table and the first table on its model page. A second, unlabeled model-page table lists 1/0.25/4; verify its meaning before changing Standard rates.",
    "gpt-5.6-cyber and gpt-daybreak-red-latest retain their previous long-context rule for history. Their model pages cap input at 272K. The Cyber page describes a premium above that limit, while the pricing table lists no rates for that tier. Bedrock lists only short-context rates for GPT-5.6 Cyber.",
    "For gpt-6-cyber, up to 272K input tokens the published rates are 20/100/2 USD per MTok for input/output/cache reads, with writes at 25 (30m) or 50 (12h). Above 272K they are 40/150/4 with neither write rate published. Schema 1 would also double the write rate, so this ID has no entry pending clarification.",
    "Max and Ultra cost 100 and 200 USD/month on the web. The former Max 20x tier maps to Ultra. A profile that reports only Max uses the current monthly Max price. Monthly API credits claimed in Claude Console are separate from the usage limits shared by Claude and Claude Code. Team seat types and Enterprise usage charges have no single monthly equivalent.",
    "Pro has no monthly comparison because plan_type pro does not distinguish the published 100, 200 and 500 USD subscriptions.",
    "Codex plan_type business does not identify seat type or billing cycle. Standard seats cost 20 USD per month billed annually or 25 billed monthly. Eligible ChatGPT Pro and Business subscriptions can claim separate API credits.",
    "gpt-6-astra and gpt-6.1-sol Ultrafast cost 6x Standard and require app support for a separate speed tier. Schema 1 only represents Standard and Fast.",
    "gpt-5.3-codex-spark retired from Codex on 2026-09-14 with no published OpenAI API price. Its existing gpt-5.3-codex family fallback (1.75/0.175/14 for input/cache reads/output) is not verified; schema 1 cannot exclude one ID from a family. The gpt-oss models have no direct OpenAI token price. The deprecations page names gpt-5-codex-mini as a replacement but provides no model-specific rate.",
    "gpt-5.4-cyber retired on 2026-10-01 and is still within the 91-day history window, but no token price is published in the reviewed official pages. It remains unpriced.",
    "GPT-6 Rosalind, the GPT-6 flagships and GPT-5.6 models publish 30-minute and 12-hour cache writes. The 12-hour rate is twice the 30-minute rate. The Codex reader supplies a single write count, so the estimate uses the 30-minute rate.",
    "Codex and ChatGPT Work included usage has different speed multipliers (2.5x Fast and 8x Ultrafast) from the API. GPT-6.1 Sol subscription usage has no long-context surcharge.",
    "Bedrock model and inference-profile IDs use the equivalent direct API value. AWS bills by endpoint, region and service tier, including regional and GovCloud premiums. Azure gpt-35-turbo requires the snapshot version because 0125 and 1106 have different prices. User-defined deployment names may also hide the model.",
    "OpenCode identifies the Decisions endpoint as gpt-6-luna-decision. Its output is free at both context lengths. Direct OpenAI requests use gpt-6-luna for both Decisions and ordinary generation, so the endpoint is needed to distinguish them when the ID alone is recorded.",
    "OpenCode Zen now redirects to OpenCode Console Models. Console is pay-as-you-go with prepaid workspace credits and no seat fee; credit purchases add 4.6% plus 0.31 USD. These fees are not token prices and are not included in this list.",
    "OpenCode Console lists 1.07/0.107/8.50 USD per MTok for input/cache reads/output on gpt-5, gpt-5-codex, gpt-5.1 and gpt-5.1-codex, versus 1.25/0.125/10 direct. Sonnet 5.5 cache reads now match the direct rate of 0.10. Console lists gpt-5.3-codex-spark at 1.75/0.175/14 with no published direct OpenAI price.",
    "Foundry -fast deployments are already in Fast mode. Their entries use the full Fast rates even when the request has no speed field.",
    "OpenCode Go costs 10 USD/month, Go Plus 40 USD/month, and Go Teams 20 USD/member/month. For each of gpt-6-luna, gpt-5.6-luna and claude-haiku-5-5, monthly included usage is 15/60/20 USD respectively across those plans, with 20% available per five hours and 50% per week. Their published token rates match the direct APIs. Extra Usage can charge the Console balance after an allowance is exhausted; it starts enabled on Go Teams. Schema 1 does not represent these plans or allowances.",
    "OpenCode initially prefers the list's API value for a known model, even over a recorded zero; unknown models can use a recorded charge. Positive reported fallback charges already stored are preserved during repricing. Neither path reconstructs Go allowance consumption or the full provider invoice.",
    "Copilot uses GitHub AI Credits at 0.01 USD each. Pro costs 10 USD/month with 1500 included credits (1000 base plus 500 flex); Pro+ costs 39 with 7000 (3900 plus 3100); Max costs 100 with 20000 (10000 plus 10000). Free and Student have unspecified credit allowances in the reviewed tables. Flex allotments can change and credits do not roll over.",
    "Copilot Business costs 19 USD/seat/month and contributes 1900 credits to a shared pool; Enterprise costs 39 and contributes 3900. Copilot access has no included allowance: it has no additional seat charge for licensed GitHub Enterprise Cloud users or costs 10 USD/seat/month for Copilot Standalone. Additional usage is billed at the published token rates after allowances are exhausted, subject to budgets. These plans and credit pools are not supported by the app's plan objects.",
    "Copilot prices gpt-5.6-luna long context above 200K input tokens, versus 272K in the direct OpenAI API. The app uses the direct API threshold. Copilot's paid-plan auto-selection discount is 10% in Chat and cloud agent; Fusion has a 30% discount through 2026-11-30. Review after that date. The app does not apply these discounts, credits or GitHub Actions charges for code review.",
    "Existing annual Copilot Pro/Pro+ subscriptions may retain legacy request-based billing: 300/1500 premium requests monthly, 0.04 USD per additional request, and model-specific request multipliers. Those multipliers are not API fast-mode prices and must not be stored as fastMultiplier.",
    "Models from other manufacturers, including Gemini, Grok, MAI-Code, Jev, Kimi, GLM, DeepSeek, Qwen, MiniMax, MiMo, Muse, Mistral, LongCat, Step, Hy and Nemotron, have no direct Anthropic/OpenAI price. OpenCode lists Gemini 4 Carbon and Argon at 50% off through 2026-11-30 and Gemini 3.6/3.7/3.8 Flash at 50% off through 2026-12-31. Copilot lists Gemini 4 Carbon and Argon promotions until 2026-12-01 and Gemini 3.8 Flash through 2026-12-31."
  ],
